        <!-- ===== Legend ===== -->
        <mxCell id="legend" value="Notation&#10;&#8226; Filled circle = initial pseudostate (start of lifecycle)&#10;&#8226; Circle-in-circle = final pseudostate (end of lifecycle)&#10;&#8226; Rounded rectangle = state&#10;&#8226; Solid arrow, label = trigger / role that causes the transition&#10;&#8226; Dashed grey arrow = terminal (dead-end) path back to the final state, no further transitions defined&#10;&#8226; Self-loop on active = repeatable transition (each rental payment)&#10;&#10;Colour key: blue = entry &#183; amber = staff review / valuation &#183; green = positive progression to completion &#183; red = rejected &#183; grey = declined by customer" style="text;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;rounded=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#cccccc;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="900" y="230" width="300" height="260" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="note" value="Source: ARCHITECTURE.md &#167;9.19 lifecycle diagram. No disbursed/closed states — a lease has no disbursement. Step order (down_payment &#8594; vehicle_purchased &#8594; registered) is load-bearing: the institution's money never chases an unmade commitment, and rentals never begin before the CR names the lessor as absolute owner." style="text;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=10;fontStyle=2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
